#  Braket notation pack (04 section 2.4, emath-r3-braket-pack-fdby):
#  kets, bras, bra-ket products, projectors, and sandwiches on the REAL
#  2-level discrete carrier. Glyphs are opt-in at the mount; the inner
#  product desugars to the admitted `dot` (sesquilinear conjugation is
#  the identity on real entries), projectors to constant matrices, and
#  the sandwich to the double sum. The pack law — ⟨ψ|ψ⟩ >= 0 and real —
#  holds by construction on this carrier. Unmounted glyphs refuse
#  (negative: tests/invalid/r3_braket_ket_unmounted.emath).
use sci::physics::notation::braket(convention = physics)

emath function braket_demo:
    definitions:
        psi = (|0⟩ + |1⟩) * (1.0 / sqrt(2.0))
        P1 = |1⟩⟨1|
        p1 = ⟨psi|P1|psi⟩
        ortho = ⟨0|1⟩
